ng with the timeline in the  past and present for the last two  seasons you'd think the nameless five  has earned some time to kick back and  relax a little of course he could if he  was in the right reality after figuring  out what kind of mess he and his  siblings have wandered into this time it  looks like the time-traveling rebel of  the family is finally giving up his old  threads and trying something new on  precise in the new trailer a brief  moment shows five looking more like a  private investigator than a member of  the umbrella academy chances are that  after the first encounter with the  sparrows he and the rest of the  umbrellas are in the wind trying to keep  off the sparrow's radar might he be  ditching his classic score uniform to  keep a low profile or is five finally  making a change for the better  near the end of the trailer pogo the  chimpanzee makes a brief appearance when  last we saw pogo he was dead impaled on  a set of antlers hanging on the umbrella  academy parlour wall the new timeline  the trailer introduces makes his return  possible but it remains to be seen how  he is brought back into the lives of the  umbrella academy students his return is  clearly meant to be the promo's big  reveal with just a quick shot of klaus  offering a spoiler alert between pogo's  appearance and the end of the trailer  also back from the dead is ben  hargreaves although he is now part of  the rival sparrow academy this is the  umbrella academy wrong again  this  is the sparrow academy  the trailer picks up where season 2  ended with the umbrella academy siblings  jumping safely back from 1964 to 2019 to  discover that ben and their father  reginald are alive again and the sparrow  academy has replaced them in their home  after the sparrow academy students are  introduced we mostly see them fighting  with their umbrella academy counterparts  one character pursues the umbrella  academy team through a hallway with the  help of an army of conjured crows and  